node_modules
.DS_Store
.gemini-gate/
# The whole .claude/ directory is working state, never shipped kit content: lane files, the
# failure log, chip discharge/repair artifacts (verdict-laden — one `git add -A` from tracked),
# harness worktrees, local settings. The shipped-docs test walk skips it for the same reason.
.claude/

# What `bin/init.mjs` appends to an ADOPTER's .gitignore, named here too. The blanket rule above
# already covers the .claude/ ones, so these four add nothing to git's behaviour in this checkout —
# and that redundancy is the point. What the kit's own layout hides, no check run inside the kit can
# see: a sensor whose output file no adopter ignored shipped in a release because here it was
# trivially ignored by `.claude/` and nobody looked at an adopter's file. Naming the families makes
# the next such divergence a line missing from a diff instead of a discovery in someone's repo.
# `tests/kit-adopter-ignores.test.mjs` runs the installer into a scratch adopter, reads the file it
# produced there, and reddens when this list falls behind it.
#
# lane declaration, ledger and pre-send rung sidecar — per-session working state
.claude/task-lane.json
.claude/lane-ledger.jsonl
.claude/brief-rung.json
# the token ledger's metrics dir — per-turn rows carrying session and task ids
.claude/metrics/
# the PM pair (v2.35.0) is PER-CHECKOUT: committed, it travels on a branch into other checkouts
.claude/kit.pair.json
# .codex/hooks.json is PER-CHECKOUT: it bakes this checkout's absolute path into every hook command.
# Committed, it registers hooks at a path other clones do not have, and a hook that fails to start
# blocks nothing, silently. The rest of .codex/ stays tracked. This one is NOT redundant here —
# nothing else in this file covers it.
.codex/hooks.json

# Thread-restart digests — transient handoffs, stale within hours; commit one only on purpose.
thread-restarts/
